  "reason": "The current best is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) with 0.619 accuracy / 0.610 F1, only modestly above the strong RNA-only multiprofile avgpool baseline, while image-only ResNet50 is weak. This leaves uncertainty about whether the image branch is limited by its encoder. config_024 changes only the image encoder to ImageNet ViT-L while keeping profile, aggregation, and concat fusion fixed, directly testing image representation. It is the best next budget use because it is a clean exploitation of the best setting and can clarify whether a stronger visual encoder can materially improve multimodal performance before further fusion or RNA-encoder changes."
